<p id="A3.SS2.SSS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">for almost surely <math id="A3.SS2.SSS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The above equation implies that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx73" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex171"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex171.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Biggr\{\frac{\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})}{\|\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})\|+\tau_{V}}:j\in\tilde{K}_{i}\Biggr\}=\Biggr\{\frac{\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}^{*}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}^{*}_{j})}{\|\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}^{*}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}^{*}_{j})\|+\tau_{V}}:j\in\tilde{K}_{i}\Biggr\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">{</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Biggr\{\frac{\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})}{\|\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})\|+\tau_{V}}:j\in\tilde{K}_{i}\Biggr\}=\Biggr\{\frac{\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}^{*}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}^{*}_{j})}{\|\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}^{*}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}^{*}_{j})\|+\tau_{V}}:j\in\tilde{K}_{i}\Biggr\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">for any <math id="A3.SS2.SSS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[\tilde{m}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[\tilde{m}]</annotation></semantics></math> and for almost surely <math id="A3.SS2.SSS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the activation functions <math id="A3.SS2.SSS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are algebraically independent, the above result indicates that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex172"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex172.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{\tilde{m}}\sum_{j\in\tilde{K}_{i}}\exp{(c_{j})}\delta_{({\bm{B}}_{j},{\bm{A}}_{j})}=\sum_{i=1}^{\tilde{m}}\sum_{j\in\tilde{K}_{i}}\exp{(c_{j}^{*})}\delta_{({\bm{B}}_{j}^{*},{\bm{A}}_{j}^{*})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{\tilde{m}}\sum_{j\in\tilde{K}_{i}}\exp{(c_{j})}\delta_{({\bm{B}}_{j},{\bm{A}}_{j})}=\sum_{i=1}^{\tilde{m}}\sum_{j\in\tilde{K}_{i}}\exp{(c_{j}^{*})}\delta_{({\bm{B}}_{j}^{*},{\bm{A}}_{j}^{*})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS2.p4.4" class="ltx_p">As a consequence, <math id="A3.SS2.SSS2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{G}\equiv\widetilde{G}_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>≡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{G}\equiv\widetilde{G}_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and the proof is completed.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ C.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ DoRAN: Stabilizing Weight-Decomposed Low-Rank Adaptation via Noise Injection and Auxiliary Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We recall that <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{X}}_{1},{\bm{Y}}_{1}),({\bm{X}}_{2},{\bm{Y}}_{2}),\ldots,({\bm{X}}_{n},{\bm{Y}}_{n})\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{X}}_{1},{\bm{Y}}_{1}),({\bm{X}}_{2},{\bm{Y}}_{2}),\ldots,({\bm{X}}_{n},{\bm{Y}}_{n})\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. samples from the following regression model:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx75" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex173"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex173.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{Y}}_{i}=f_{G_{*}}({\bm{X}}_{i})+\varepsilon_{i},\quad i=1,2,\ldots,n," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{Y}}_{i}=f_{G_{*}}({\bm{X}}_{i})+\varepsilon_{i},\quad i=1,2,\ldots,n,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the Gaussian noises <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{1},\ldots,\varepsilon_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{1},\ldots,\varepsilon_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. and satisfy that <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[{\varepsilon_{i}}|{\bm{X}}_{i}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[{\varepsilon_{i}}|{\bm{X}}_{i}]=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}(\varepsilon_{i}|{\bm{X}}_{i})=\sigma^{2}I_{\bar{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}(\varepsilon_{i}|{\bm{X}}_{i})=\sigma^{2}I_{\bar{d}}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f_{G_{*}}(.)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{G_{*}}(.)</annotation></semantics></math> admits the following form:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx76" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex174"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex174.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{G_{*}}(\bm{X}):=\sum_{j=1}^{L}\frac{\exp\left(\bm{X}^{\top}m_{Q,j}\frac{\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{W}^{*}_{2,j}\bm{B}^{*}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{W}^{*}_{1,j}\bm{A}^{*}_{j})}{\|\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{W}^{*}_{2,j}\bm{B}^{*}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{W}^{*}_{1,j}\bm{A}^{*}_{j})\|+\tau_{Q}}\bm{C}_{K}\bm{X}+c^{*}_{j}\right)}{S(\bm{X})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{G_{*}}(\bm{X}):=\sum_{j=1}^{L}\frac{\exp\left(\bm{X}^{\top}m_{Q,j}\frac{\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{W}^{*}_{2,j}\bm{B}^{*}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{W}^{*}_{1,j}\bm{A}^{*}_{j})}{\|\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{W}^{*}_{2,j}\bm{B}^{*}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{W}^{*}_{1,j}\bm{A}^{*}_{j})\|+\tau_{Q}}\bm{C}_{K}\bm{X}+c^{*}_{j}\right)}{S(\bm{X})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 113.81102pt\times\left(m_{V,j}\frac{\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{W}^{*}_{2,j}\bm{B}^{*}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{W}^{*}_{1,j}\bm{A}^{*}_{j})}{\|\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{W}^{*}_{2,j}\bm{B}^{*}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{W}^{*}_{1,j}\bm{A}^{*}_{j})\|+\tau_{V}}\right)\bm{X}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="11.602em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 113.81102pt\times\left(m_{V,j}\frac{\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{W}^{*}_{2,j}\bm{B}^{*}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{W}^{*}_{1,j}\bm{A}^{*}_{j})}{\|\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{W}^{*}_{2,j}\bm{B}^{*}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{W}^{*}_{1,j}\bm{A}^{*}_{j})\|+\tau_{V}}\right)\bm{X},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A3.EGx77" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S(\bm{X})=\sum_{k=1}^{L}\exp\left(\bm{X}^{\top}m_{Q,k}\frac{\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{W}^{*}_{2,j}\bm{B}^{*}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{W}^{*}_{1,j}\bm{A}^{*}_{j})}{\|\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{W}^{*}_{2,j}\bm{B}^{*}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{W}^{*}_{1,j}\bm{A}^{*}_{j})\|+\tau_{Q}}\bm{C}_{K}\bm{X}+c^{*}_{k}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S(\bm{X})=\sum_{k=1}^{L}\exp\left(\bm{X}^{\top}m_{Q,k}\frac{\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{W}^{*}_{2,j}\bm{B}^{*}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{W}^{*}_{1,j}\bm{A}^{*}_{j})}{\|\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{W}^{*}_{2,j}\bm{B}^{*}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{W}^{*}_{1,j}\bm{A}^{*}_{j})\|+\tau_{Q}}\bm{C}_{K}\bm{X}+c^{*}_{k}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The least-square estimator <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> takes the following form:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx78" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex175"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex175.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G_{n}:=\textnormal{arg}\min_{G\in\mathcal{G}_{L^{\prime}}(\Theta)}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\|{\bm{Y}}_{i}-f_{G}({\bm{X}}_{i})\|^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mtext>arg</mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mmultiscripts><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mstyle><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G_{n}:=\textnormal{arg}\min_{G\in\mathcal{G}_{L^{\prime}}(\Theta)}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\|{\bm{Y}}_{i}-f_{G}({\bm{X}}_{i})\|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">From the Gaussianity assumption of <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{i}|{\bm{X}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{i}|{\bm{X}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Y}}_{i}|{\bm{X}}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(f_{G_{*}}({\bm{X}}_{i}),\sigma^{2}I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Y}}_{i}|{\bm{X}}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(f_{G_{*}}({\bm{X}}_{i}),\sigma^{2}I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the least square estimator <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is indeed equivalent to a maximum likelihood estimator with respect to the data <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{1}|{\bm{X}}_{1},\ldots,Y_{n}|{\bm{X}}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{1}|{\bm{X}}_{1},\ldots,Y_{n}|{\bm{X}}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, which has the following form:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx79" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex176"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex176.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G_{n}\in\argmax_{G\in\mathcal{G}_{L^{\prime}}(\Theta)}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\log(p({\bm{Y}}_{i}|f_{G}({\bm{X}}_{i}),\sigma^{2}I_{\bar{d}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G_{n}\in\argmax_{G\in\mathcal{G}_{L^{\prime}}(\Theta)}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\log(p({\bm{Y}}_{i}|f_{G}({\bm{X}}_{i}),\sigma^{2}I_{\bar{d}}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{Y}}_{i}|f_{G}({\bm{X}}_{i}),\sigma^{2}I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{Y}}_{i}|f_{G}({\bm{X}}_{i}),\sigma^{2}I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> stands for multivariate Gaussian distribution with mean <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{G}({\bm{X}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{G}({\bm{X}})</annotation></semantics></math> and covariance matrix <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}I_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}I_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we will denote some useful notations to help us quantify the distance between the two density functions, <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\bm{Y}|f_{G_{n}}({\bm{X}}),\sigma^{2}I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{Y}|f_{G_{n}}({\bm{X}}),\sigma^{2}I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\bm{Y}|f_{G_{*}}({\bm{X}}),\sigma^{2}I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{Y}|f_{G_{*}}({\bm{X}}),\sigma^{2}I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall the set of all mixing measure <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{L}(\Theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{L}(\Theta)</annotation></semantics></math> and denote the set of regression function <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{L}:=\{f_{G}(x):G\in\mathcal{G}_{L}(\Theta)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{L}:=\{f_{G}(x):G\in\mathcal{G}_{L}(\Theta)\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{L}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the set of conditional density of all mixing measures in <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{L}(\Theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{L}(\Theta)</annotation></semantics></math>, and we further denote,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx80" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex177"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex177.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\mathcal{P}}_{L}(\Theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\mathcal{P}}_{L}(\Theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex177.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\{p_{(G+G_{*})/2}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}}):G\in\mathcal{G}_{L}(\Theta)\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\{p_{(G+G_{*})/2}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}}):G\in\mathcal{G}_{L}(\Theta)\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex178"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex178.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\mathcal{P}}_{L}^{1/2}(\Theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\mathcal{P}}_{L}^{1/2}(\Theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex178.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\{p^{1/2}_{(G+G_{*})/2}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}}):G\in\mathcal{G}_{L}(\Theta)\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\{p^{1/2}_{(G+G_{*})/2}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}}):G\in\mathcal{G}_{L}(\Theta)\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Also, for each <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the Hellinger ball in <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{P}}_{L}^{1/2}(\Theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{P}}_{L}^{1/2}(\Theta)</annotation></semantics></math> centered around the conditional density <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{G_{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{G_{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex179" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex179.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{P}}_{L}^{1/2}(\Theta,\delta):=\{p^{1/2}\in\tilde{\mathcal{P}}_{L}^{1/2}(\Theta):h(p,p_{G_{*}})\leq\delta\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{P}}_{L}^{1/2}(\Theta,\delta):=\{p^{1/2}\in\tilde{\mathcal{P}}_{L}^{1/2}(\Theta):h(p,p_{G_{*}})\leq\delta\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">To measure the size of the above sets, we leverage the following quantity from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>]</cite>:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx81" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{J}(\delta,\tilde{\mathcal{P}}^{1/2}_{L}(\Theta,\delta)):=\int_{\delta^{2}/2^{13}}^{\delta}H_{B}^{1/2}(t,\tilde{\mathcal{P}}^{1/2}_{L}(\Theta,t),\|\cdot\|_{\mathcal{L}^{2}(\mu)})dt\vee\delta," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>13</mn></msup></mrow><mi>δ</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{J}(\delta,\tilde{\mathcal{P}}^{1/2}_{L}(\Theta,\delta)):=\int_{\delta^{2}/2^{13}}^{\delta}H_{B}^{1/2}(t,\tilde{\mathcal{P}}^{1/2}_{L}(\Theta,t),\|\cdot\|_{\mathcal{L}^{2}(\mu)})dt\vee\delta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H_{B}(t,\tilde{\mathcal{P}}^{1/2}_{L}(\Theta,t),\|\cdot\|_{\mathcal{L}^{2}(\mu)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{B}(t,\tilde{\mathcal{P}}^{1/2}_{L}(\Theta,t),\|\cdot\|_{\mathcal{L}^{2}(\mu)})</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the bracketing entropy of <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{P}}^{1/2}_{L}(\Theta,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{P}}^{1/2}_{L}(\Theta,t)</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm, while <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\vee\delta=\max(t,\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\vee\delta=\max(t,\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>. By adapting the proof argument of Theorem 7.4 and Theorem 9.2 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>]</cite>, we have the following lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the function
<math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi(\delta)\geq\mathcal{J}(\delta,\mathcal{P}^{1/2}_{HL}(\Theta,\delta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi(\delta)\geq\mathcal{J}(\delta,\mathcal{P}^{1/2}_{HL}(\Theta,\delta))</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi(\delta)/\delta^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi(\delta)/\delta^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a non-increasing function of <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for some universal constant <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> and sequence <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\delta_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\delta_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{n}\delta_{n}^{2}\geq c\Psi(\delta_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{n}\delta_{n}^{2}\geq c\Psi(\delta_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex180" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex180.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left(\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{X}}}[h(p_{\hat{G}_{n}}(\cdot|{\bm{X}}),p_{G_{*}}(\cdot|{\bm{X}}))]&gt;\delta\right)\leq c\exp\left(-\frac{n\delta^{2}}{\nu^{2}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝑿</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left(\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{X}}}[h(p_{\hat{G}_{n}}(\cdot|{\bm{X}}),p_{G_{*}}(\cdot|{\bm{X}}))]&gt;\delta\right)\leq c\exp\left(-\frac{n\delta^{2}}{\nu^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for all <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\geq\delta_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\geq\delta_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The goal is to upper bound the bracketing entropy for any <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\epsilon\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\epsilon\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx82" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle H_{B}(\epsilon,\tilde{\mathcal{P}}^{1/2}_{HL}(\Theta,\epsilon),\|\cdot\|_{\mathcal{L}^{2}(\mu)})\lesssim\log(1/\epsilon)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H_{B}(\epsilon,\tilde{\mathcal{P}}^{1/2}_{HL}(\Theta,\epsilon),\|\cdot\|_{\mathcal{L}^{2}(\mu)})\lesssim\log(1/\epsilon).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">We will prove this bound later. Given this bound, it follows that,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx83" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{B}(\delta,\tilde{\mathcal{P}}^{1/2}_{HL}(\Theta,\delta))\lesssim\int_{\delta^{2}/2^{13}}^{\delta}\log(1/t)dt\vee\delta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>13</mn></msup></mrow><mi>δ</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{B}(\delta,\tilde{\mathcal{P}}^{1/2}_{HL}(\Theta,\delta))\lesssim\int_{\delta^{2}/2^{13}}^{\delta}\log(1/t)dt\vee\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Consider <math id="A3.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi(\delta)=\delta\cdot[\log(1/\delta)]^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi(\delta)=\delta\cdot[\log(1/\delta)]^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the it is obvious that <math id="A3.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi(\delta)/\delta^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi(\delta)/\delta^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-increasing function of <math id="A3.SS3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. In addition, equation <a href="#A3.E28" title="In C.3 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ DoRAN: Stabilizing Weight-Decomposed Low-Rank Adaptation via Noise Injection and Auxiliary Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a> implies that <math id="A3.SS3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi(\delta)\geq\mathcal{J}_{B}(\delta,\tilde{\mathcal{P}}^{1/2}_{HL}(\Theta,\delta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi(\delta)\geq\mathcal{J}_{B}(\delta,\tilde{\mathcal{P}}^{1/2}_{HL}(\Theta,\delta))</annotation></semantics></math>. By choosing <math id="A3.SS3.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{n}=\sqrt{\log(n)/n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{n}=\sqrt{\log(n)/n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A3.SS3.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{n}\delta_{n}^{2}\geq c\Psi(\delta_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{n}\delta_{n}^{2}\geq c\Psi(\delta_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> for some universal constant <math id="A3.SS3.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>. An application of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ C.3 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ DoRAN: Stabilizing Weight-Decomposed Low-Rank Adaptation via Noise Injection and Auxiliary Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> leads us to the conclusion of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ C.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ DoRAN: Stabilizing Weight-Decomposed Low-Rank Adaptation via Noise Injection and Auxiliary Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A3.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(p(\bm{Y}|g_{\bar{G}_{n}}({\bm{X}}),\sigma^{2}I_{d}),p(\bm{Y}|g_{\bar{G}_{*}}({\bm{X}}),\sigma^{2}I_{d}))=\mathcal{O}(\sqrt{\log(n)/n})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(p(\bm{Y}|g_{\bar{G}_{n}}({\bm{X}}),\sigma^{2}I_{d}),p(\bm{Y}|g_{\bar{G}_{*}}({\bm{X}}),\sigma^{2}I_{d}))=\mathcal{O}(\sqrt{\log(n)/n}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Hellinger distance. Hellinger distance between two multivariate normal distributions has the following closed-form,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx84" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex181"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex181.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h(p(\bm{Y}|g_{\bar{G}_{n}}({\bm{X}}),\sigma^{2}I_{d}),p(\bm{Y}|g_{\bar{G}_{*}}({\bm{X}}),\sigma^{2}I_{d}))=1-\exp\left\{-\dfrac{1}{8\sigma^{2}}\|g_{\bar{G}_{n}}({\bm{X}})-g_{\bar{G}_{*}}({\bm{X}})\|^{2}\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h(p(\bm{Y}|g_{\bar{G}_{n}}({\bm{X}}),\sigma^{2}I_{d}),p(\bm{Y}|g_{\bar{G}_{*}}({\bm{X}}),\sigma^{2}I_{d}))=1-\exp\left\{-\dfrac{1}{8\sigma^{2}}\|g_{\bar{G}_{n}}({\bm{X}})-g_{\bar{G}_{*}}({\bm{X}})\|^{2}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, for sufficient large <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists some universal constant <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A3.Ex182" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex182.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{\bar{G}_{n}}({\bm{X}})-g_{\bar{G}_{*}}({\bm{X}})\|^{2}\leq 8\sigma^{2}\log\left(\dfrac{1}{1-C\log(n)/n}\right)\leq 16\sigma^{2}C\log(n)/n." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{\bar{G}_{n}}({\bm{X}})-g_{\bar{G}_{*}}({\bm{X}})\|^{2}\leq 8\sigma^{2}\log\left(\dfrac{1}{1-C\log(n)/n}\right)\leq 16\sigma^{2}C\log(n)/n.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p11.2" class="ltx_p">As a consequence, we have</p>
<table id="A3.Ex183" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex183.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{\bar{G}_{n}}({\bm{X}})-g_{\bar{G}_{*}}({\bm{X}})\|=\mathcal{O}(\sqrt{\log(n)/n})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{\bar{G}_{n}}({\bm{X}})-g_{\bar{G}_{*}}({\bm{X}})\|=\mathcal{O}(\sqrt{\log(n)/n}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p11.3" class="ltx_p">or <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{\bar{G}_{n}}-g_{\bar{G}_{*}}\|_{L^{2}(\mu)}=\mathcal{O}_{P}(\sqrt{\log(n)/n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{\bar{G}_{n}}-g_{\bar{G}_{*}}\|_{L^{2}(\mu)}=\mathcal{O}_{P}(\sqrt{\log(n)/n})</annotation></semantics></math>. This concludes the proof of this proposition.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Now we go back to prove the upper bound at equation <a href="#A3.E27" title="In C.3 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ DoRAN: Stabilizing Weight-Decomposed Low-Rank Adaptation via Noise Injection and Auxiliary Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>. First we derive an upper bound for the multivariate Gaussian density <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{G}(\cdot|{\bm{X}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{G}(\cdot|{\bm{X}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the variance effect <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed, we have</p>
<table id="A3.Ex184" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex184.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{G}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})=\dfrac{1}{(2\pi\sigma^{2})^{d/2}}\exp\left(-\dfrac{\|\bm{Y}-f_{G}({\bm{X}})\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right)\leq\dfrac{1}{(2\pi\sigma^{2})^{d/2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒀</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{G}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})=\dfrac{1}{(2\pi\sigma^{2})^{d/2}}\exp\left(-\dfrac{\|\bm{Y}-f_{G}({\bm{X}})\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right)\leq\dfrac{1}{(2\pi\sigma^{2})^{d/2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p12.2" class="ltx_p">Because the input space <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and parameter space <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> are both bounded, there exists a constant <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{G}({\bm{X}})\|\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{G}({\bm{X}})\|\leq M</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\in\mathcal{G}_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\in\mathcal{G}_{L}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{X}}\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{X}}\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, for any <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bm{Y}\|\geq 2M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bm{Y}\|\geq 2M</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A3.EGx85" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex185"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex185.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\|\bm{Y}-g_{G}({\bm{X}})\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\geq\frac{\|\bm{Y}\|^{2}}{8\sigma^{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒀</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\|\bm{Y}-g_{G}({\bm{X}})\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\geq\frac{\|\bm{Y}\|^{2}}{8\sigma^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p12.3" class="ltx_p">which leads to</p>
<table id="A3.Ex186" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex186.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\bm{Y}|g_{G}({\bm{X}}),\sigma^{2}I_{\bar{d}})=\dfrac{1}{(2\pi\sigma^{2})^{d/2}}\exp\left(-\dfrac{\|\bm{Y}-g_{G}({\bm{X}})\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right)\leq\dfrac{1}{(2\pi\sigma^{2})^{d/2}}\exp\left(-\frac{\|\bm{Y}\|^{2}}{8\sigma^{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒀</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{Y}|g_{G}({\bm{X}}),\sigma^{2}I_{\bar{d}})=\dfrac{1}{(2\pi\sigma^{2})^{d/2}}\exp\left(-\dfrac{\|\bm{Y}-g_{G}({\bm{X}})\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right)\leq\dfrac{1}{(2\pi\sigma^{2})^{d/2}}\exp\left(-\frac{\|\bm{Y}\|^{2}}{8\sigma^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p12.4" class="ltx_p">We define the integrable function</p>
<table id="A3.Ex187" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex187.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})=\begin{cases}(2\pi\sigma^{2})^{-d/2}&amp;\quad\text{ for }\|\bm{Y}\|\leq 2M,\\
(2\pi\sigma^{2})^{-d/2}\exp\left(-\dfrac{\|\bm{Y}\|^{2}}{8\sigma^{2}}\right)&amp;\quad\text{ for }\|\bm{Y}\|&gt;2M,\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext> for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>exp</mi><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext> for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})=\begin{cases}(2\pi\sigma^{2})^{-d/2}&amp;\quad\text{ for }\|\bm{Y}\|\leq 2M,\\
(2\pi\sigma^{2})^{-d/2}\exp\left(-\dfrac{\|\bm{Y}\|^{2}}{8\sigma^{2}}\right)&amp;\quad\text{ for }\|\bm{Y}\|&gt;2M,\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p12.5" class="ltx_p">and thus <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\bm{Y}|g_{G}({\bm{X}}),\sigma^{2}I_{d})\leq K(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{Y}|g_{G}({\bm{X}}),\sigma^{2}I_{d})\leq K(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{X}}\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{X}}\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&lt;\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&lt;\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{e_{1},\ldots,e_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{e_{1},\ldots,e_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>-cover of <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{L}(\Theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{L}(\Theta)</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm such that the covering number <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="N:=N(\tau,\mathcal{P}_{L}(\Theta),\|\cdot\|_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N:=N(\tau,\mathcal{P}_{L}(\Theta),\|\cdot\|_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Next, we construct the brackets of the form <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[L_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}}),U_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[L_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}}),U_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})]</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq N</annotation></semantics></math> with</p>
<table id="A3.EGx86" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex188"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex188.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex188.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\max\{e_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})-\tau,0\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\max\{e_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})-\tau,0\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex189"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex189.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex189.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\max\{e_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})+\tau,K(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\max\{e_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})+\tau,K(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p13.2" class="ltx_p">It is straightforward to check that <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{L}(\Theta)\subset\bigcup_{i=1}^{N}[L_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}}),U_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">⊂</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{L}(\Theta)\subset\bigcup_{i=1}^{N}[L_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}}),U_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})-L_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})\leq\min\{\eta,K(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})-L_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})\leq\min\{\eta,K(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})\}</annotation></semantics></math>. From this, we can achieve the following upper bound</p>
<table id="A3.EGx87" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex190"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex190.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|U_{i}-L_{i}\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|U_{i}-L_{i}\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex190.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\|\bm{Y}\|\leq 2M}|U_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})-L_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})|d({\bm{X}},\bm{Y})+\int_{\|\bm{Y}\|&gt;2M}|U_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})-L_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})|d({\bm{X}},\bm{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\|\bm{Y}\|\leq 2M}|U_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})-L_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})|d({\bm{X}},\bm{Y})+\int_{\|\bm{Y}\|&gt;2M}|U_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})-L_{i}(\bm{Y}|{\bm{X}})|d({\bm{X}},\bm{Y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex191"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex191.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq K\tau+\exp\left(-\dfrac{K^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right)\leq K^{\prime}\tau," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq K\tau+\exp\left(-\dfrac{K^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right)\leq K^{\prime}\tau,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p13.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K:=\max\{2M,\sqrt{8\sigma^{2}}\}\log(1/\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K:=\max\{2M,\sqrt{8\sigma^{2}}\}\log(1/\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be a positive constant. From the definition of bracket entropy, given that <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H_{B}(K^{\prime}\tau,\mathcal{P}_{L}(\Theta),\|\cdot\|_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{B}(K^{\prime}\tau,\mathcal{P}_{L}(\Theta),\|\cdot\|_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> is the logarithm of the smallest number of bracket of size <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}\tau</annotation></semantics></math> necessary to cover <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{L}(\Theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{L}(\Theta)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A3.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H_{B}(K^{\prime}\tau,\mathcal{P}_{L}(\Theta),\|\cdot\|_{1})\leq\log(N)=\log N(\tau,\mathcal{P}_{L}(\Theta),\|\cdot\|_{1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{B}(K^{\prime}\tau,\mathcal{P}_{L}(\Theta),\|\cdot\|_{1})\leq\log(N)=\log N(\tau,\mathcal{P}_{L}(\Theta),\|\cdot\|_{1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p14.1" class="ltx_p">Now we want to bound the covering number <math id="A3.SS3.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, we denote <math id="A3.SS3.p14.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta=\{{\bm{B}}_{j},{\bm{A}}_{j},c_{j}:({\bm{B}}_{j},{\bm{A}}_{j},c_{j})\in\Theta\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=\{{\bm{B}}_{j},{\bm{A}}_{j},c_{j}:({\bm{B}}_{j},{\bm{A}}_{j},c_{j})\in\Theta\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Because the parameter space <math id="A3.SS3.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> is compact, <math id="A3.SS3.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is also a compact set. Thus, we can find <math id="A3.SS3.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>-covers <math id="A3.SS3.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.SS3.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta_{\tau}|\leq\mathcal{O}(\tau^{-2rdL-L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta_{\tau}|\leq\mathcal{O}(\tau^{-2rdL-L})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p15.1" class="ltx_p">For each mixing measure <math id="A3.SS3.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=\sum_{j=1}^{L}\exp(c_{j})\delta_{({\bm{B}}_{j},{\bm{A}}_{j})}\in\mathcal{G}_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=\sum_{j=1}^{L}\exp(c_{j})\delta_{({\bm{B}}_{j},{\bm{A}}_{j})}\in\mathcal{G}_{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider an other mixing measure as follows,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx88" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G^{\prime}=\sum_{j=1}^{L}\exp(c_{j}^{\prime})\delta_{({\bm{B}}_{j}^{\prime},{\bm{A}}_{j}^{\prime})}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G^{\prime}=\sum_{j=1}^{L}\exp(c_{j}^{\prime})\delta_{({\bm{B}}_{j}^{\prime},{\bm{A}}_{j}^{\prime})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p15.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS3.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c_{j}^{\prime},{\bm{B}}_{j}^{\prime},{\bm{A}}_{j}^{\prime})\in\Delta_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c_{j}^{\prime},{\bm{B}}_{j}^{\prime},{\bm{A}}_{j}^{\prime})\in\Delta_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> is the closest to <math id="A3.SS3.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c_{j},{\bm{B}}_{j},{\bm{A}}_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c_{j},{\bm{B}}_{j},{\bm{A}}_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>. We define some following intermediate functions to alleviate the bound:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx89" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex192"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex192.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{1}(\bm{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{1}(\bm{X})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex192.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\sum_{j=1}^{L}\mathrm{softmax}\Bigg(\bm{X}^{\top}m_{Q,j}\frac{\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})}{\|\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})\|+\tau_{Q}}\bm{X}+c_{j}\Bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\sum_{j=1}^{L}\mathrm{softmax}\Bigg(\bm{X}^{\top}m_{Q,j}\frac{\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})}{\|\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})\|+\tau_{Q}}\bm{X}+c_{j}\Bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex193"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex193.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 71.13188pt\left(m_{V,j}\frac{\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})}{\|\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})\|+\tau_{V}}\right)\bm{X}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 71.13188pt\left(m_{V,j}\frac{\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})}{\|\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})\|+\tau_{V}}\right)\bm{X},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex194"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex194.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{2}(\bm{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{2}(\bm{X})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex194.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\sum_{j=1}^{L}\mathrm{softmax}\Bigg(\bm{X}^{\top}m_{Q,j}\frac{\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})}{\|\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})\|+\tau_{Q}}\bm{X}+c_{j}^{\prime}\Bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\sum_{j=1}^{L}\mathrm{softmax}\Bigg(\bm{X}^{\top}m_{Q,j}\frac{\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})}{\|\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})\|+\tau_{Q}}\bm{X}+c_{j}^{\prime}\Bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex195"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex195.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 71.13188pt\left(m_{V,j}\frac{\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})}{\|\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})\|+\tau_{V}}\right)\bm{X}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 71.13188pt\left(m_{V,j}\frac{\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})}{\|\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})\|+\tau_{V}}\right)\bm{X},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p16.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we have,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx90" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex196"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex196.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|f-f_{1}\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|f-f_{1}\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex196.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{j=1}^{L}\sup_{{\bm{X}}\in\mathcal{X}}\mathrm{softmax}\Bigg(\bm{X}^{\top}m_{Q,j}\frac{\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})}{\|\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})\|+\tau_{Q}}\bm{X}+c_{j}\Bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{j=1}^{L}\sup_{{\bm{X}}\in\mathcal{X}}\mathrm{softmax}\Bigg(\bm{X}^{\top}m_{Q,j}\frac{\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})}{\|\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})\|+\tau_{Q}}\bm{X}+c_{j}\Bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex197"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex197.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 39.83368pt\times m_{V,j}||\mathbf{V}_{j}\bm{X}-\mathbf{V}^{\prime}_{j}\bm{X}||" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="4.202em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 39.83368pt\times m_{V,j}||\mathbf{V}_{j}\bm{X}-\mathbf{V}^{\prime}_{j}\bm{X}||</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex198"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex198.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{j=1}^{L}\sup_{{\bm{X}}\in\mathcal{X}}m_{V,j}||\mathbf{V}_{j}\bm{X}-\mathbf{V}^{\prime}_{j}\bm{X}||" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{j=1}^{L}\sup_{{\bm{X}}\in\mathcal{X}}m_{V,j}||\mathbf{V}_{j}\bm{X}-\mathbf{V}^{\prime}_{j}\bm{X}||</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex199"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex199.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{j=1}^{L}\sup_{{\bm{X}}\in\mathcal{X}}m_{V,j}\left\|\left(\frac{\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})}{\|\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})\|+\tau_{V}}-\frac{\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})}{\|\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})\|+\tau_{V}}\right)\bm{X}\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{j=1}^{L}\sup_{{\bm{X}}\in\mathcal{X}}m_{V,j}\left\|\left(\frac{\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})}{\|\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})\|+\tau_{V}}-\frac{\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})}{\|\bm{C}_{V}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})\|+\tau_{V}}\right)\bm{X}\right\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex200"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex200.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\sum_{j=1}^{L}\sup_{{\bm{X}}\in\mathcal{X}}\|({\bm{B}}_{j},{\bm{A}}_{j})-({\bm{B}}_{j}^{\prime},{\bm{A}}_{j}^{\prime})\|\cdot\|{\bm{X}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\sum_{j=1}^{L}\sup_{{\bm{X}}\in\mathcal{X}}\|({\bm{B}}_{j},{\bm{A}}_{j})-({\bm{B}}_{j}^{\prime},{\bm{A}}_{j}^{\prime})\|\cdot\|{\bm{X}}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\sum_{j=1}^{L}\tau\cdot B\lesssim\tau," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\sum_{j=1}^{L}\tau\cdot B\lesssim\tau,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p16.2" class="ltx_p">where the second last inequality holds due to the fact that the input space is bounded: <math id="A3.SS3.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bm{X}\|\leq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bm{X}\|\leq B</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.SS3.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{X}}\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{X}}\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p17.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly, we also have,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx91" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex201"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex201.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|f_{1}-f_{2}\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|f_{1}-f_{2}\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex201.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{j=1}^{L}\sup_{{\bm{X}}\in\mathcal{X}}\Bigg|\mathrm{softmax}\Bigg(\bm{X}^{\top}m_{Q,j}\frac{\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})}{\|\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})\|+\tau_{Q}}\bm{X}+c_{j}\Bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>softmax</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{j=1}^{L}\sup_{{\bm{X}}\in\mathcal{X}}\Bigg|\mathrm{softmax}\Bigg(\bm{X}^{\top}m_{Q,j}\frac{\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})}{\|\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})\|+\tau_{Q}}\bm{X}+c_{j}\Bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex202"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex202.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 42.67912pt-\mathrm{softmax}\Bigg(\bm{X}^{\top}m_{Q,j}\frac{\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})}{\|\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})\|+\tau_{Q}}\bm{X}+c_{j}^{\prime}\Bigg)\Bigg|\cdot m_{V,j}\|\mathbf{V}_{j}^{\prime}\bm{X}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>softmax</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 42.67912pt-\mathrm{softmax}\Bigg(\bm{X}^{\top}m_{Q,j}\frac{\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})}{\|\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})\|+\tau_{Q}}\bm{X}+c_{j}^{\prime}\Bigg)\Bigg|\cdot m_{V,j}\|\mathbf{V}_{j}^{\prime}\bm{X}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex203"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex203.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\sum_{j=1}^{L}\sup_{{\bm{X}}\in\mathcal{X}}\Bigg|\mathrm{softmax}\Bigg(\bm{X}^{\top}m_{Q,j}\frac{\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})}{\|\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})\|+\tau_{Q}}\bm{X}+c_{j}\Bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≲</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>softmax</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\sum_{j=1}^{L}\sup_{{\bm{X}}\in\mathcal{X}}\Bigg|\mathrm{softmax}\Bigg(\bm{X}^{\top}m_{Q,j}\frac{\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})}{\|\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j})\|+\tau_{Q}}\bm{X}+c_{j}\Bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex204"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex204.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 42.67912pt-\mathrm{softmax}\Bigg(\bm{X}^{\top}m_{Q,j}\frac{\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})}{\|\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})\|+\tau_{Q}}\bm{X}+c_{j}^{\prime}\Bigg)\Bigg|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>softmax</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 42.67912pt-\mathrm{softmax}\Bigg(\bm{X}^{\top}m_{Q,j}\frac{\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})}{\|\bm{C}_{Q}+\sigma_{2}(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime})\sigma_{1}(\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime})\|+\tau_{Q}}\bm{X}+c_{j}^{\prime}\Bigg)\Bigg|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex205"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex205.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≲</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex205.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{j=1}^{L}\|(\bm{B}_{j},\bm{A}_{j},c_{j})-(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime},\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime},c_{j}^{\prime})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{j=1}^{L}\|(\bm{B}_{j},\bm{A}_{j},c_{j})-(\bm{B}_{j}^{\prime},\bm{A}_{j}^{\prime},c_{j}^{\prime})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≲</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\&gt;\tau." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\&gt;\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p18.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, by triangle inequality, we have <math id="A3.SS3.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f-f_{2}\|_{\infty}\lesssim\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≲</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f-f_{2}\|_{\infty}\lesssim\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, by noting that the Gaussian density function <math id="A3.SS3.p18.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f(x)=(2\pi\sigma^{2})^{-d/2}\exp\left(-\|x\|^{2}/2\sigma^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=(2\pi\sigma^{2})^{-d/2}\exp\left(-\|x\|^{2}/2\sigma^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is a global Lipschitz function, we have,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx92" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|p(\bm{Y}|f_{G}({\bm{X}}),\sigma^{2}I_{d})-p(\bm{Y}|f_{G^{\prime}}({\bm{X}}),\sigma^{2}I_{d})\|_{1}\lesssim\|g_{G}({\bm{X}})-g_{\bar{G}}({\bm{X}})\|_{\infty}\lesssim\tau." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≲</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≲</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|p(\bm{Y}|f_{G}({\bm{X}}),\sigma^{2}I_{d})-p(\bm{Y}|f_{G^{\prime}}({\bm{X}}),\sigma^{2}I_{d})\|_{1}\lesssim\|g_{G}({\bm{X}})-g_{\bar{G}}({\bm{X}})\|_{\infty}\lesssim\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p19.1" class="ltx_p">From the definition of covering number, we get</p>
<table id="A3.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log N(\tau,\mathcal{P}_{HL}(\Theta),\|\cdot\|_{1})\leq|\Delta_{\tau}|\leq\mathcal{O}(\tau^{-2rdL-L})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log N(\tau,\mathcal{P}_{HL}(\Theta),\|\cdot\|_{1})\leq|\Delta_{\tau}|\leq\mathcal{O}(\tau^{-2rdL-L})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p19.2" class="ltx_p">From equations <a href="#A3.E30" title="In C.3 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ DoRAN: Stabilizing Weight-Decomposed Low-Rank Adaptation via Noise Injection and Auxiliary Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a> and <a href="#A3.E35" title="In C.3 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ DoRAN: Stabilizing Weight-Decomposed Low-Rank Adaptation via Noise Injection and Auxiliary Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>, we have</p>
<table id="A3.Ex206" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex206.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H_{B}(\tau,\mathcal{P}_{L}(\Theta),\|\cdot\|_{1})\lesssim\log(1/\xi)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{B}(\tau,\mathcal{P}_{L}(\Theta),\|\cdot\|_{1})\lesssim\log(1/\xi).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p19.3" class="ltx_p">By choosing <math id="A3.SS3.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi=\epsilon/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi=\epsilon/2</annotation></semantics></math>, we achieve that</p>
<table id="A3.Ex207" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex207.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{B}(\epsilon,\mathcal{P}_{HL}(\Theta),h)\lesssim\log(1/\epsilon)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{B}(\epsilon,\mathcal{P}_{HL}(\Theta),h)\lesssim\log(1/\epsilon).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p19.4" class="ltx_p">This concludes our proof.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Use of Large Language Models</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, large language models were utilized exclusively for editorial assistance, such as grammar correction and spelling improvements, and were not applied to content creation, data analysis, or experimental design.</p>
</div>
</section>
